Why: Linux launches keep the user's front window: launched apps get a startup id whose user time predates every user action, so window managers with focus-stealing prevention (mutter, KWin) map them behind; a window manager that focuses the new window anyway is undone by the X11 focus guard, and the reply and its active field say what moved and whether it was handed back.

